## solar-noon

solar-noon-ask = At what time by the clock does the true noon come?
solar-noon-title = A gnomon: the noon, the clock and the latitude
solar-noon-choices = At 12:00 sharp — that is what noon is
solar-noon-choices-2 = Later than 12:00
solar-noon-choices-3 = Earlier than 12:00
solar-noon-place-label = City
solar-noon-build-question = 20 March 2026 is the spring equinox. In a school yard ({ $name }) we stand a metre stick — a gnomon — upright and measure its shadow with a tape every half hour by the local clock. The shortest shadow is the true noon: the Sun stands highest of the day. At what time by the clock will it come?
solar-noon-setup = A metre stick (a gnomon), a plumb line to stand it upright, a tape measure, a clock (the local time)
